{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7076742","formula":"C₁₄H₈O₁₀","hill":"C14H8O10","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":8.0,"O":10.0},"names":{"en":"Octahydroxyanthraquinone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Octahydroxyanthraquinone is an organic compound with formula C14H8O10, formally derived from anthraquinone by replacement of 8 hydrogen atoms by hydroxyl groups. The compound was obtained in 1911 by Georg von Georgievics and can be obtained through oxidation of rufigallol (1,2,3,5,6,7-hexahydroxyanthraquinone) with boric acid and mercuric oxide in sulfuric acid at 250 °C (482 °F). Esters of octahydroxyanthraquinone, where all eight hydroxyls are replaced by straight-chain 1-alkanecarboxylate groups H3C-(CH2)n-COO-, with n between 6 and 14, are liquid crystals and have been studied for possible LCD applications."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":9840703,"mass":336.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"C12=C(C(=C(C(=C1O)O)O)O)C(=O)C3=C(C2=O)C(=C(C(=C3O)O)O)O","inchikey":"KOWBNNJAGJIIJW-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8-octahydroxyanthracene-9,10-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9840703","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":-2.672,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.672,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":2.546,"y":-2.76,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.546,"y":-2.76,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":2.546,"y":2.76,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.546,"y":2.76,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":4.878,"y":-1.375,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.878,"y":-1.374,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":4.878,"y":1.375,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.878,"y":1.375,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.273,"y":0.698,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.273,"y":-0.698,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.273,"y":0.698,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.273,"y":-0.698,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":-1.448,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.447,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.48